From: j7 g3d
Subject: j7prime: G3D probe must not sweep the PMU page

j7gpu=2|3 (0302) printed every non-zero word of PMU+0x4040..0x407c. On the phone it read
PMU+4040/4044/4048 fine and then panicked on PMU+404c: "Unclassified kernel abort
(fault_code=0x10)", esr 0x96000210, far = mapping base + 0x4c. That is a synchronous external
abort from a hole in the PMU register file. Read only G3D config (+0x60) and status (+0x64).

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/A5XELTEGPU.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/A5XELTEGPU.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/A5XELTEGPU.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/A5XELTEGPU.cpp
@@ -291,12 +291,11 @@
         service->setProperty("J7G3DProbeResult", "pmu-map-failed");
         return;
     }
-    for (vm_offset_t off = 0x40; off < 0x80; off += 4) {
-        uint32_t v = a5g3d_read32(pmu, off);
-        if (v) {
-            IOLog("J7 G3D: PMU+%04x=%08x\n", (unsigned)(0x4000 + off), v);
-        }
-    }
+    /*
+     * Do NOT sweep this page: the PMU has holes that raise a synchronous external abort
+     * (the first J7 trial panicked reading PMU+404c, fault_code 0x10, far = page + 0x4c).
+     * Read only the two registers this probe needs.
+     */
     uint32_t config = a5g3d_read32(pmu, 0x60);
     uint32_t status = a5g3d_read32(pmu, 0x64);
     service->setProperty("J7G3DPMUConfig", static_cast<uint64_t>(config), 32);
